# 38. V0 Dependency Policy

## Core

Aim for the smallest practical set:

```text
Bun 1.4.x
Cordis
@bufbuild/protobuf
@connectrpc/connect
```

## Cognitive implementation

```text
selected RuVector packages
@ruvector/rvf / appropriate RVF binding
```

Prefer narrow RuVector packages over the umbrella package where feasible.

## UI

```text
react
react-dom
@astryxdesign/core
@astryxdesign/theme-neutral
```

Include StyleX only where required by the selected Astryx distribution path.

## Optional interoperability

```text
@ag-ui/core
@ag-ui/proto or encoder as required
MCP SDK
A2A implementation
provider SDKs
```

## Development

```text
fast-check
playwright
protobuf/buf generation tooling
```

Use `bun:test` rather than introducing another general test runner unless a concrete limitation requires one.

---

# 39. Dependency Maturity Policy

Cordis, Astryx, RuVector and RVF are active external projects.

The Framework SHALL therefore:

* pin exact tested versions;
* update through controlled dependency PRs;
* maintain compatibility tests around behavioral contracts;
* prevent third-party types from leaking across public abstraction boundaries;
* maintain fallback implementations for core interfaces;
* avoid depending on undocumented internals unless isolated inside one adapter;
* record the exact dependency versions used to produce releases.

RuVector and RVF in particular are evolving rapidly; the Framework gains their functionality without making their implementation architecture part of its own identity.

---

# 40. Architectural Acceptance Criteria

The architecture is considered validated only if all of the following are true.

### A. Cordis can be removed conceptually

Application code imports no Cordis runtime types.

### B. RuVector can be deleted operationally

Deleting cognitive state does not destroy truth or authorization state.

### C. `.sea` does not know the Framework exists

No framework-specific grammar is required.

### D. DomainForge remains independently releasable

Framework integration is an adapter.

### E. RealityTrace remains independently releasable

Framework integration is an evidence adapter.

### F. Astryx can be replaced

Headless and React APIs remain valid.

### G. Connect can be replaced

The service contract survives transport changes.

### H. AG-UI can be removed

Native Framework execution and UI remain functional.

### I. Learning cannot expand authority

Adaptive systems operate only inside deterministic eligibility.

### J. A Copilot-like application can be composed

No Copilot-specific kernel primitives are introduced.

### K. A Harness-like system can be composed

No Harness-specific kernel primitives are introduced.

### L. The cognitive system can improve without semantic mutation

New learned rankings and memories do not require `.sea` grammar changes.

### M. Runtime behavior is causally inspectable

Events, fibers, capabilities, semantic references and RealityTrace observations can be correlated.

---

# 41. Definition of the Framework

The Framework can be summarized as:

> A Bun-native semantic application substrate in which dynamically composed capabilities execute through scoped, reversible lifecycles; durable facts form an authoritative event history; unfinished work is represented explicitly as continuations; DomainForge projects existing `.sea` semantics into the runtime without language changes; RealityTrace receives correlated execution evidence; RuVector provides rebuildable cognitive recall and adaptive ranking; RVF provides portable cognitive state and branching; Protobuf and Connect expose typed cross-language boundaries; and headless clients, AG-UI, React and Astryx project the same underlying system into user-facing applications.

The central dependency chain is therefore:

```text
                     .sea
                      │
                 DomainForge
                      │
                      ▼
             SEMANTIC PROJECTION
                      │
                      ▼
                 FRAMEWORK
          ┌───────────┼────────────┐
          │           │            │
       Cordis      SQLite      RealityTrace
     execution      truth        evidence
          │           │
          └─────┬─────┘
                ▼
             RuVector
             cognition
                │
                ▼
               RVF
       portable cognition

                │
        ┌───────┴─────────┐
        ▼                 ▼
 Protobuf / Connect     AG-UI
        │                 │
        └───────┬─────────┘
                ▼
         Headless Client
                │
             React
                │
             Astryx
```

The architectural rule that governs the entire design is:

> **Semantics constrain execution. Events preserve truth. Cognition discovers relevance. Evidence records reality. Representations remain replaceable.**
